   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_QbHt7twm8sQ28k4N",
   "name": "Area under a Velocity-Time Graph",
   "definition": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Area under a velocity-time graph"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Velocity-time graphs show the speed and direction of an object in motion over a specific period of **time**\n- The **area** under a velocity-time graph is equal to the **displacement** of a moving object"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The area under a graph can be sectioned into triangles and rectangles to make the calculations easier\n- The area of a triangle can be found with the following formula:"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "$A_{triangle}=\\frac{1}{2}bh$"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The area of a rectangle can be found with the following formula:"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "$A_{rectangle}=bh$"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Where:\n\n  - $A$ = area\n  - $b$ = length of base\n  - $h$ = height"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "worked-example",
   "label": "Worked Example",
   "md": "The velocity-time graph of a vehicle travelling with uniform acceleration is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![v-t Area Worked Example (1), downloadable AS & A Level Physics revision notes](assets/fbb274e6e673-v-t-area-worked-example-1.png)\n\nCalculate the displacement of the vehicle at 40 s.\n\n**Answer:**\n\n**Step 1: State how to determine the displacement**\n\n- The displacement is equal to the area under a velocity-time graph\n\n**Step 2: Determine the scale on the graph**\n\n- Each division is $\\frac{50}{10}=5\\mathrm{km}h^{-1}$\n\n![2-1-3-we-v-t-answer-cie-new](assets/5170d9313423-2-1-3-we-v-t-answer-cie-new.png)\n\n**Step 3: Determine the base and height of the graph**\n\n- Time = base = 40 s\n- Velocity = height = 105 km h<sup>–1</sup>\n\n**Step 4: Convert km h**<sup>**-1**</sup>** into km s**<sup>**–1**</sup>\n\n$\\frac{105}{60\\times60}=0.0292\\mathrm{km}s^{-1}$\n\n**Step 5: Calculate the area under the graph**\n\nArea of a right-angled triangle =  $\\frac{1}{2}\\timesbase\\timesheight$\n\n$Area=\\frac{1}{2}\\times40\\times0.0292=0.6\\mathrm{km}$"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "Always check the values given on the y-axis of a motion graph - students often confuse displacement-time graphs and velocity-time graphs."
  }
 ]
}